        "original_id": "b4eb2b51-9f50-5c29-9b52-f5ea6b6c17b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards\n- Places: Dublin, Ireland; The Point\n- People: Ronan Keating; Mariah Carey; Britney Spears; Marilyn Manson; Iggy Pop; Brian Hugh Warner\n- Groups: The Cardigans; Jamiroquai; The Corrs\n- Songs: \"Heartbreaker\"; \"...Baby One More Time\"; \"(You Drive Me) Crazy\"\n- Roles: host; performer; show opener\n\nFacts:\n- The 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards were held in Dublin, Ireland, at The Point.\n- Ronan Keating returned as host of the 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards.\n- Mariah Carey performed \"Heartbreaker\" at the 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards.\n- Britney Spears performed \"...Baby One More Time\" and \"(You Drive Me) Crazy\" at the 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards.\n- Iggy Pop was the show opener at the 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards.\n- The Cardigans, Jamiroquai, Marilyn Manson, and The Corrs performed at the 1999 MTV Europe Music Awards.\n- Brian Hugh Warner, born January 5, 1969, is professionally known as Marilyn Manson.\n- Marilyn Manson is an American singer, songwriter, musician, composer, actor, painter, author, and former music journalist.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
